# patching-hosts host knob (CannObserv/broker#67). Grammar: the vendored
# skill's references/knob.md. The skill reads this file and never writes it.
# Times are UTC. A malformed line makes the host report-only until fixed.

class production
posture scheduled

# --- when -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The owner's monthly window: Monday 23:00 to Tuesday 05:00 (Mon 16:00-22:00
# PT), set 2026-10-13. Every step's whole span must fit inside it, clear of the
# quiet ranges below, or apply.sh refuses it.
window Mon 23:00-05:00

# broker-backup.timer: OnCalendar=hourly, RandomizedDelaySec=5min,
# AccuracySec=1min, so a run starts up to 6 min past the hour and takes about
# a second. No step may share it: it reads dump.rdb, which a Redis stop rewrites.
quiet 00:00-00:07
quiet 01:00-01:07
quiet 02:00-02:07
quiet 03:00-03:07
quiet 04:00-04:07
quiet 05:00-05:07
quiet 06:00-06:07
quiet 07:00-07:07
quiet 08:00-08:07
quiet 09:00-09:07
quiet 10:00-10:07
quiet 11:00-11:07
quiet 12:00-12:07
quiet 13:00-13:07
quiet 14:00-14:07
quiet 15:00-15:07
quiet 16:00-16:07
quiet 17:00-17:07
quiet 18:00-18:07
quiet 19:00-19:07
quiet 20:00-20:07
quiet 21:00-21:07
quiet 22:00-22:07
quiet 23:00-23:07
# broker-bus-health.timer is OnUnitActiveSec=10min: its ticks drift, so no
# quiet range can avoid them. It is WARN-only, so a tick inside a step is
# harmless; a Redis step is best started just after one.

# --- the data store -------------------------------------------------------
datastore redis redis-server
# The hourly snapshot to gs://co-gcs-broker-backup stands in for a dump. Under
# appendonly yes a restored RDB is ignored unless staged as the AOF base:
# docs/RECOVERY.md, src/broker/restore.py.
backup broker-backup.service redis-server.service

# tailscaled carries every participant's connection, and redis-server binds
# the tailnet address (After=/Wants= tailscaled, wait-for-tailnet-addr.sh), so
# a tailscaled restart is a bus event: its own held step, after the redis one.
# Followed in the maintenance lane (owner, 2026-10-13); its postinst restarts
# tailscaled, so the step is approved on its own and the bind checked after.
origin pkgs.tailscale.com follow
hold tailscale tailscale

# --- who is told ----------------------------------------------------------
# Each bus participant (docs/STREAMS.md, docs/NETWORK-PATHS.md).
caller CannObserv/archiver
caller CannObserv/watcher
caller CannObserv/replicator
caller CannObserv/processor
# The fifth, the ACL user `provisioner` (live 2026-10-12), has no line: its
# repo is private and this one is public, so the line would publish its name
# (gregoryfoster/skills#350, as for image-owner). It is told by hand, on its
# own tracker, and checked in every Redis step like the four above.

# --- checks (never root: they run as the invoking user, here exedev) -------
# Redis answers, and anonymous is still refused. NOAUTH writes no ACL LOG
# entry (measured 2026-10-13), so polling it every second adds no evidence noise.
health redis-cli -h 127.0.0.1 -p 6379 PING 2>&1 | grep -qx 'NOAUTH Authentication required.'
# The tailnet bind every remote participant connects through.
health ss -Hltn 'sport = :6379' | grep -q '100\.97\.91\.19:6379'
# The probe's last tick is recent and clean. 12 min: OnUnitActiveSec=10min,
# and the widest gap measured over two days was 660 s. A stale last line fails.
health journalctl -u broker-bus-health.service --since -12min -o cat --no-pager | grep '"Bus health summary"' | tail -n 1 | grep -q '"finding_count": 0'

# No inflight line: nothing a non-root command can read sees a consumer
# mid-batch. Every consumer runs on its own host, and pending counts need
# acladmin, which is root through systemd-creds. The probe's pending-age and
# group-undelivered findings are the after-the-fact signal.

# --- exceptions -----------------------------------------------------------
# The restarter scan can't follow a uv-run module. Neither starts or restarts
# a unit: the backup uploads dump.rdb, and the probe is WARN-only and reports
# to co-status (src/broker/backup.py, src/broker/bus_health.py).
exception not-restarter:broker-backup.service 2027-04-13 uploads dump.rdb to GCS; starts and restarts no unit
exception not-restarter:broker-bus-health.service 2027-04-13 WARN-only probe reporting to co-status; starts and restarts no unit
